  "markdown_content": "OpenAI is working with former Twitter India head Rishi Jaitly as a senior advisor to facilitate talks with the government about AI policy, TechCrunch has exclusively learned. OpenAI is also looking to set up a local team in India.\\n\\nThe move comes as the artificial intelligence company seeks to expand its presence in one of the world's largest digital markets. Jaitly's role will primarily focus on engaging with government officials and policymakers to discuss AI regulation and implementation frameworks.\\n\\nThis strategic appointment signals OpenAI's serious intentions to establish a strong foothold in India, where artificial intelligence adoption is rapidly growing across various sectors including:\\n\\n* Technology\\n* Healthcare\\n* Education",
